+  # ---- /images, /hero, /cats hold pictures and nothing else ----
+  # script-src 'self' trusts every same-origin URL that answers with JavaScript, and the
+  # media mount under /images/products is written by an upload route. That route accepts
+  # only PNG/JPEG/WebP, but the folder's own .htaccess blocks PHP-like names and nothing
+  # more: an x.html, x.svg, x.xhtml, x.xml or x.js placed there by any other route (File
+  # Manager, a future import tool) was served as an active document or a script. Measured:
+  # text/html, image/svg+xml, application/xhtml+xml, application/xml, text/javascript.
+  # Two layers, because either alone leaves a gap:
+  #   * the policy for these folders is "sandbox": opened as a page the file gets an opaque
+  #     origin, no scripts, no forms, no access to the shop's storage; <img> is unaffected.
+  #   * the active extensions are refused outright, so nothing here can be <script src>'d.
+  # A <FilesMatch> is inherited by subfolders (the media mount's own .htaccess cannot undo it)
